Package: nlFit
Title: Fit the Ordinal Model of Number-Line Estimation
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Dale J.", "Cohen",
           email = "cohend@uncw.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3353-3340"))
Description: Simulates and fits the ordinal model of number-line estimation
    described in Thompson and Cohen (2025) <doi:10.1037/amp0001617>. In the
    model a participant places each target ordinally between the estimates
    they remember and the reference points they can see, with parameters for
    the spatial bias of an unanchored placement, the length of the memory
    window, the resolution with which numbers near a landmark are
    discriminated, the weight given to accurate responding, and the
    probability that a conceptual landmark is available. Provides the
    simulation, a fit statistic for use with a grid search, and reporting of
    the fitted parameters and fit statistics. Handles the bounded, unbounded
    and universal number-line tasks.
